From: DKR-R Win95 port
Subject: [PATCH] Count the drains, and stop asking the environment per message

The queue trace reports 108,794 requeues of one message value against 7,723
deposits of it. Fourteen retries per deposit is not a finding: a requeue is one
retry per *drain*, so the same figure describes a message blocked for fourteen
drains and a message spun on. Only the number of drains tells them apart, and
nothing was counting them.

The priority pass at the head of `dequeue_external_messages` is counted with
them. It empties the external queue and refills it on every call, copying every
pending message -- each holding a `shared_ptr`, hence an atomic pair per copy --
before the loop below drains it a second time. Its cost scales with how often the
function is entered, which is the quantity that was missing.

And the two trace blocks asked `std::getenv("DKR_TRACE_SP")` on **every message
that passes through**, switched off or not. Over a run reaching a thousand
display lists that is more than two hundred thousand scans of the environment
block for an answer that cannot change. The rest of this port reads a switch into
a `static const bool` for exactly that reason; this file predates the habit.

A diagnostic that is off should cost nothing, and this one was not free.

--- a/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
+++ b/ultramodern/src/mesgqueue.cpp
@@ -189,6 +189,31 @@
 
 bool do_send(RDRAM_ARG PTR(OSMesgQueue) mq_, OSMesg msg, bool jam, bool block);
 
+// **A trace that is switched off must cost nothing per message.**
+//
+// The two blocks below used to ask `std::getenv("DKR_TRACE_SP")` on every message
+// that passes through here, which on a run reaching a thousand display lists is
+// over two hundred thousand scans of the environment block for an answer that
+// cannot change. The rest of this port reads its switches into a `static const
+// bool` for exactly that reason; this file had been written before that was the
+// habit.
+static const bool trace_sp = std::getenv("DKR_TRACE_SP") != nullptr;
+
+// **What the requeues actually cost, in calls rather than in messages.**
+//
+// The totals below report 108,794 requeues of one message value against 7,723
+// deposits of it -- fourteen retries per deposit -- and that ratio says nothing
+// on its own. A requeue is one retry per *drain*, so the same figure describes a
+// message blocked for fourteen drains and a genuine spin, and only the number of
+// drains tells them apart.
+//
+// The priority pass at the head of the function is counted with it: it empties
+// the queue and refills it on every call, copying every pending message --
+// each holding a `shared_ptr`, hence an atomic pair per copy -- before the loop
+// below drains it a second time. That is the part whose cost scales with how
+// often the function is entered, and nothing was measuring it.
+static unsigned long drains = 0, priority_moves = 0;
+
 void dequeue_external_messages(RDRAM_ARG1) {
     if (exited.load()) {
         throw ultramodern::thread_terminated{};
@@ -211,11 +236,13 @@
     // events whose relative order is not guaranteed. Serving them first is
     // therefore faithful, and it suffices to lift them out of starvation. Their
     // order among themselves is preserved - that is the one the game observes.
+    drains++;
     {
         std::vector<QueuedMessage> all{};
         while (external_messages.try_dequeue(to_send)) {
             all.push_back(to_send);
         }
+        priority_moves += (unsigned long)all.size();
         std::stable_partition(all.begin(), all.end(), [](const QueuedMessage& m) {
             return m.source == ultramodern::EventMessageSource::Sp ||
                    m.source == ultramodern::EventMessageSource::Dp;
@@ -263,8 +290,7 @@
         // symbol map. Hard-coding it would not be acceptable elsewhere; here it
         // is a diagnostic behind an environment variable, and the only way to
         // ask the question.
-        if (to_send.source == ultramodern::EventMessageSource::Dp &&
-            std::getenv("DKR_TRACE_SP") != nullptr) {
+        if (to_send.source == ultramodern::EventMessageSource::Dp && trace_sp) {
             static unsigned nulls = 0, set = 0, shown = 0;
             /* The guest RDRAM is stored byte-swapped on the host side: we read
                the word backwards to recover the game's value. */
@@ -290,7 +316,7 @@
         // A crash on Windows 95 finds `curRSPTask` null in `__scHandleRSP`, while
         // a single task has been submitted and a single `sp_complete` called. If
         // the count below exceeds that one, the question is settled.
-        if (std::getenv("DKR_TRACE_SP") != nullptr) {
+        if (trace_sp) {
             static unsigned deposits = 0, refusals = 0, requeues = 0;
             if (sent) { deposits++; } else if (to_send.requeue_if_blocked) { requeues++; }
             else { refusals++; }
@@ -339,6 +365,10 @@
                                  "[trace][mq] total msg=0x%08X deposited=%u refused=%u requeued=%u\n",
                                  seen[m][0], tot[m][0], tot[m][1], tot[m][2]);
                 }
+                // The denominator the ratios above are missing.
+                std::fprintf(stderr,
+                             "[trace][mq] drains=%lu priority-copies=%lu\n",
+                             drains, priority_moves);
                 // Force the log onto the disk: Windows 95 only updates the size
                 // at close time, so a frozen program leaves a zero-byte file
                 // whatever it wrote. Without this call, "the program stopped
